		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_K_UJPTAMVGD410B59C4140AFC8FA">
			<name>F1-003 Trailblazer launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F1-003 Trailblazer launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/eCeQpU

Launch - 03-Aug-08 - Falcon 1 Flight 3 - RTS Omelek

First stage recontacted the second stage engine after stage separation due to transient thrust, because of residual fuel evaporation in M1C engine
First flight of Merlin 1C engine on the 1st stage

Trailblazer (83.5kg), PRESat (4kg), NanoSail-D (4kg), Celestis-07 (7g) CubeSats payload
Planned orbit 330/685/9°

Elon Musk: "We have flight four of Falcon 1 almost ready for flight and flight five right behind that. I have also given the go ahead to begin fabrication of flight six. Falcon 9 development will also continue unabated, taking into account the lessons learned with Falcon 1. We have made great progress this past week with the successful nine engine firing."
"There should be absolutely zero question that SpaceX will prevail in reaching orbit and demonstrating reliable space transport. For my part, I will never give up and I mean never."</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_048008C3D32C6E06344C</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">F1-003 Trailblazer launch groundtrack</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/eCeQpU

Launch - 03-Aug-08 - Falcon 1 Flight 3 - RTS Omelek

First stage recontacted the second stage engine after stage separation due to transient thrust, because of residual fuel evaporation in M1C engine
First flight of Merlin 1C engine on the 1st stage

Trailblazer (83.5kg), PRESat (4kg), NanoSail-D (4kg), Celestis-07 (7g) CubeSats payload
Planned orbit 330/685/9°

Elon Musk: &quot;We have flight four of Falcon 1 almost ready for flight and flight five right behind that. I have also given the go ahead to begin fabrication of flight six. Falcon 9 development will also continue unabated, taking into account the lessons learned with Falcon 1. We have made great progress this past week with the successful nine engine firing.&quot;
&quot;There should be absolutely zero question that SpaceX will prevail in reaching orbit and demonstrating reliable space transport. For my part, I will never give up and I mean never.&quot;</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
