		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1380609923AD7668">
			<name>F1-004 Ratsat launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F1-004 Ratsat launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/eCeQpU

Launch - 28-Sep-08 - Falcon 1 Flight 4 - RTS Omelek

First successful launch of Falcon 1
Increased time between first stage burnout and second stage separation then in previous flight.

165kg Ratsat - DemoSat RTF payload
Placed to 617/635km/9.35° orbit - still attached to the second stage

Elon Musk: "The data shows we achieved a super precise orbit insertion middle of the bull's-eye and then went on to coast and restart the second stage, which was icing on the cake."
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0E597E97242C6E06344D</styleUrl>
