		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_K_UJPTAMVGD410B97EA5B83D7BC9">
			<name>F9-005	CRS-2 launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F9-005	CRS-2 launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/eCeQpU

Launch - 01-Mar-13 - Falcon 9 v1.0 Flight 5 - CCAFS SLC-40

First unpressurized cargo in trunk - HRSGF grapple bars
Total Cargo Upmass with packaging - 677kg

Dragon C104 deployed into 199/321km/51.66° orbit

When priming four Draco Thruster Pods, Dragon detected insufficient pressurization on N2O4 system of three pods - Flight Computers placed Dragon into Passive Abort Mode - Thruster system disabled, solar arrays not deployed.

@elonmusk 1 Mar 2013:
Issue with Dragon thruster pods. System inhibiting three of four from initializing. About to command inhibit override.
Pods 1 and 4 now online and thrusters engaged. Dragon transitioned from free drift to active control. Yes!!
Thruster pods one through four are now operating nominally. Preparing to raise orbit. All systems green.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0AF505CC592C6E06344F</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">F9-005	CRS-2 launch groundtrack</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/eCeQpU

Launch - 01-Mar-13 - Falcon 9 v1.0 Flight 5 - CCAFS SLC-40

First unpressurized cargo in trunk - HRSGF grapple bars
Total Cargo Upmass with packaging - 677kg

Dragon C104 deployed into 199/321km/51.66° orbit

When priming four Draco Thruster Pods, Dragon detected insufficient pressurization on N2O4 system of three pods - Flight Computers placed Dragon into Passive Abort Mode - Thruster system disabled, solar arrays not deployed.

@elonmusk 1 Mar 2013:
Issue with Dragon thruster pods. System inhibiting three of four from initializing. About to command inhibit override.
Pods 1 and 4 now online and thrusters engaged. Dragon transitioned from free drift to active control. Yes!!
Thruster pods one through four are now operating nominally. Preparing to raise orbit. All systems green.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
