		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_KFPCTKJEXBCI100AAE50F9CF89AA">
			<name>F9-009 CRS-3 water landing</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F9-009 CRS-3 water landing</div><div><b>description</b>: Estimation - Center of landing area

Water Landing - 18-Apr-14 - Falcon 9 v1.1. Flight 9

First flight with landing legs
First successful soft water landing

@elonmusk 18 Apr 2014:
Last known state for rocket boost stage is 360 m/s, Mach 1.1, 8.5 km altitude and roll rate close to zero (v important!)
Flight computers continued transmitting for 8 seconds after reaching the water. Stopped when booster went horizontal.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_02AE052A052C6E063451</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">F9-009 CRS-3 water landing</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Estimation - Center of landing area

Water Landing - 18-Apr-14 - Falcon 9 v1.1. Flight 9

First flight with landing legs
First successful soft water landing

@elonmusk 18 Apr 2014:
Last known state for rocket boost stage is 360 m/s, Mach 1.1, 8.5 km altitude and roll rate close to zero (v important!)
Flight computers continued transmitting for 8 seconds after reaching the water. Stopped when booster went horizontal.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
