		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_KFPCTKJEXBCI0F821CCC2C09D56E">
			<name>F9-014 CRS-5 ASDS position</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F9-014 CRS-5 ASDS position</div><div><b>description</b>: Hard Droneship Landing - 10-Jan-15 - Falcon 9 v1.1. Flight 14 - Marmac300 ASDS, Elsbeth III tug, Go Quest support - Landing Failure

348km downrange
Ran out of Grid fin hydraulic fluid - Crash to droneship

@elonmusk 10 Jan 2015:
Rocket made it to drone spaceport ship, but landed hard. Close, but no cigar this time. Bodes well for the future tho.
Grid fins worked extremely well from hypersonic velocity to subsonic, but ran out of hydraulic fluid right before landing.
F9 fins only work for 4 mins. We were ~10% off.
Upcoming flight already has 50% more hydraulic fluid, so should have plenty of margin for landing attempt next month.

FCC APPLICATION: https://goo.gl/TBcbK4</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0DA7032B6A2C6E063453</styleUrl>
