		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_K_UJPTAMVGD410086499651E356E">
			<name>F9-015 DSCOVR launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F9-015 DSCOVR launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/0YcgoK

Launch - 11-Feb-15 - Falcon 9 v1.1. Flight 15 - CCAFS SLC-40

570kg SEL1 Lissajous orbit satellite http://epic.gsfc.nasa.gov/
Deployment to 187/1371145km/37.09° SEL1 Transfer Orbit

@elonmusk 8 Feb 2015:
Launching our 1st deep space mission today. Headed to Earth-Sun L1 gravity null point at 1M miles, 4X further than moon.
Rocket reentry will be much tougher this time around due to deep space mission. Almost 2X force and 4X heat. Plenty of hydraulic fluid tho.

Second stage in heliocentric orbit</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_34A26ED6282C6E063453</styleUrl>
