		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1347914D8EC623E4">
			<name>F9-018 CRS-6 ASDS position</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F9-018 CRS-6 ASDS position</div><div><b>description</b>: Hard Droneship Landing - 14-Apr-15 - Falcon 9 v1.1. Flight 17 - Marmac300 JRtI, Elsbeth III tug, Go Quest support - Landing Failure

348km downrange (CRS-5 identical position)
Sticky throttle valve - overcompensating - two legs broke their stops in landing - tip over - explosion

@elonmusk 19 Apr 2015:
Cause of hard rocket landing confirmed as due to slower than expected throttle valve response. Next attempt in 2 months.
While the rocket does look rather tall & tippy, a stable landing is no problem with proper throttle response

FCC APPLICATION: https://goo.gl/Ll4X9x</div>]]></description>
