		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_133E4521DBCACD43">
			<name>F9-026 Eutelsat-117WB&amp;ABS-2A ASDS position</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: F9-026 Eutelsat-117WB&ABS-2A ASDS position</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 15-Jun-16 - Falcon 9 v1.2. Flight 26 - Marmac304 OCISLY, Elsbeth III tug, Go Quest support - Landing Failure

681km downrange (Thaicom-8 identical position)
Three-engines deceleration - slow (>6sec) central engine hovering descent (T/W=1) - LOX depletion just above (19m) the deck - hard touch-down- tip over.

@elonmusk 15 Jun 2016:
Ascent phase & satellites look good, but booster rocket had a RUD on droneship.
Looks like thrust was low on 1 of 3 landing engines. High g landings v sensitive to all engines operating at max.
@elonmusk 17 Jun 2016:
Turns out the landing was not as fast we thought, but still hard enough to destroy the primary airframe and accordion the engines
Looks like early liquid oxygen depletion caused engine shutdown just above the deck

FCC APPLICATION: https://goo.gl/AnOotA</div>]]></description>
