		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_19BEB80F4C476A7B">
			<name>M1363 NROL-76 launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1363 NROL-76 launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/umnY2Q

Launch - 01-May-17 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b3/4 Flight 33 - KSC LC-39A

First national security mission.
First flight of Block 4 S2

The NROL-76 spy satellite (USA-276) contracted by the NRO through Ball Aerospace.
Deployment to 398/401km/49.96° orbit - near ISS.

One-half of fairing parachuted into the ocean with accuracy about 7km from target and recovered intact.
Second stage performed successful 3,4 to 6 hrs coast demo.

@elonmusk 01 May 2017:
Launch and landing of the NRO spy satellite was good. Tough call, as high altitude wind shear was at 98.6% of the theoretical load limit.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_02207D65342C6E063455</styleUrl>
