		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1ADA932413C40E5A">
			<name>M1338 Iridium-2 launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1338 Iridium-2 launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/umnY2Q

Launch - 25-Jun-17 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b3/4 Flight 37 - VAFB SLC-4E

First mission with upgraded titanium grid fins (SN0003), designed to provide greater control authority and withstand high reentry heat.

Totally 9600kg payload - Iridium NEXT Satellites 113, 115, 117, 118, 120, 121, 123, 124, 126, 128 with dispenser.
Deployment to 610/625km/86.67° orbit

@elonmusk 25 Jun 2017:
Flying with larger & significantly upgraded hypersonic grid fins. Single piece cast & cut titanium. Can take reentry heat with no shielding.
Slightly heavier than shielded aluminum, but more control authority and can be reused indefinitely with no touch ups
They will, but the hydraulic system is closed loop, so no fluid lost. They do need more power & energy, but rocket has plenty of that.
Not painted, as they glow red hot during a fast reentry.
More aero effectiveness to create steep spires on windward side at the grid fin intersections
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_02207D65342C6E063455</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
