		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1AF76AA976D568D7">
			<name>M1338 Iridium-2 repositioned ASDS
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1338 Iridium-2 repositioned ASDS
</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 25-Jun-17 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b3 B1036 Flight 37 - Marmac303 JRtI, KELLY C tug, NRC Quest support

326km downrange, repositioned 56.8km to south-east

1-3-1 engines 32s boostback, 20s entry burn, with 1 engine 30s successful landing burn.
9m from bullseye landing. Engine cutoff over the deck - hard touch-down absorbed by all crush cores.

@elonmusk 25 Jun 2017:
Launch at 1:25 delivering 10 satellites for Iridium. Droneship repositioned due to extreme weather. Will be tight.
New titanium grid fins worked even better than expected. Should be capable of an indefinite number of flights with no service.
</div>]]></description>
