		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1CFC4136C91A080E">
			<name>M1339 Iridium-3 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1339 Iridium-3 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Estimated track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/ErbkUw

Launch - 09-Oct-17 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b4 Flight 42 - VAFB SLC-4E

Booster 1041, white landing leg top-inner side. AL type of grid fins.
Totally 9600kg payload - Iridium NEXT Satellites 107, 119, 122, 125, 127, 129, 132, 133, 136, 139 with dispenser.
Deployment to 612/627km/86.68° orbit

@elonmusk 09 Oct 2017:
The last of ten Iridium global communication satellites delivered to orbit several hundred miles above Earth, traveling at over 17,000 mph. They will circle the planet every 90 minutes.
</div>]]></description>
