		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1DCD83B1D1E2F03B">
			<name>M1390 Zuma initial (39a) launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1390 Zuma initial (39a) launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Estimated track inside former CX-39A hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Initially Planned Launch - 18-Nov-17 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b4 Flight 45 - KSC LC-39A

Booster 1043, AL type of grid fins, Fairing 1.0.

Secretive payload - code-named Zuma contracted by government through Northrop Grumman for U.S. government.
Postponed to 04-Jan-18 at CX-40 due to fairing issue.

@SpaceX 17 Nov 2017:
Standing down on Zuma mission to take a closer look at data from recent fairing testing for another customer.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_3B2DE56B3B2C6E06345B</styleUrl>
