		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1DD2CD1700DE0FAE">
			<name>M1389 GovSat-1 booster water landing
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1389 GovSat-1 booster water landing
</div><div><b>description</b>: Water landing - 31-Jan-18 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b3 B1032.2 Flight 48 - Go Quest support

MECO at 2316m/s, approx. 1-3-1 engines 24s entry burn, 1-3-1 engines 11s water landing.

@elonmusk 31 Jan 2018:
This rocket was meant to test very high retrothrust landing in water so it didn’t hurt the droneship, but amazingly it has survived. We will try to tow it back to shore.

Usafed floating booster was finally destroyed as there was no safe way to get it back to Port.

641km downrange

Initially planned booster recovery by Marmac304 OCISLY cancelled in favor of upcoming FH core recovery.
FCC APPLICATION: https://goo.gl/w2FV5R
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_08867DE3732C6E06345B</styleUrl>
