		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1F66C5B3FE59FB02">
			<name>M1346 FH Demo launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1346 FH Demo launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Estimated track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 06-Feb-18 - Falcon Heavy b2-b3 Flight 1 - KSC LC-39A

CC-B1033 - reused engines, AL grid fins, NY-B1025.2 -TI grid fins(SN0003), white leg inside, PY-B1023.2 -TI grid fins, white leg inside
Fairing 1.0
Demo Payload - approx.1250 kg Elon's cherry red Tesla Roadster with Starman (mannequin) in qualification article of spacesuit - attached to the second stage.
Pre TMI orbit 180/6951km/29.0°. Successful TMI burn into final heliocentric Earth-Mars trasfer orbit 0.986x1.667AU/1.05°.

@elonmusk 06 Feb 2018:
Upper stage restart nominal, apogee raised to 7000 km. Will spend 5 hours getting zapped in Van Allen belts & then attempt final burn for Mars.
@elonmusk 07 Feb 2018:
Third burn successful. Exceeded Mars orbit and kept going to the Asteroid Belt.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_05907649AE2C6E06345D</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">M1346 FH Demo launch groundtrack
</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Estimated track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 06-Feb-18 - Falcon Heavy b2-b3 Flight 1 - KSC LC-39A

CC-B1033 - reused engines, AL grid fins, NY-B1025.2 -TI grid fins(SN0003), white leg inside, PY-B1023.2 -TI grid fins, white leg inside
Fairing 1.0
Demo Payload - approx.1250 kg Elon&apos;s cherry red Tesla Roadster with Starman (mannequin) in qualification article of spacesuit - attached to the second stage.
Pre TMI orbit 180/6951km/29.0°. Successful TMI burn into final heliocentric Earth-Mars trasfer orbit 0.986x1.667AU/1.05°.

@elonmusk 06 Feb 2018:
Upper stage restart nominal, apogee raised to 7000 km. Will spend 5 hours getting zapped in Van Allen belts &amp; then attempt final burn for Mars.
@elonmusk 07 Feb 2018:
Third burn successful. Exceeded Mars orbit and kept going to the Asteroid Belt.
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
