		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1FA700D31E385993">
			<name>M1400 Paz launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1400 Paz launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Estimated track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 22-Feb-18 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b3/4 Flight 49 - VAFB SLC-4E

First flight with fairing 2.0.
Sooty expendable legless booster 1038.2, AL type of grid fins.

Totally 2150kg payload - 1350kg Paz (ex SEOSAR) satellite with two 400kg Starlink demo satellites MicroSat-2a/2b (Tintin A/B)

Deployment into 497/517km/97.46° sun-synchronous dawn-dusk orbit

@elonmusk 22 Feb 2018:
First two Starlink demo satellites, called Tintin A & B, deployed and communicating to Earth stations
Tintin A & B will attempt to beam “hello world” in about 22 hours when they pass near LA
Don’t tell anyone, but the wifi password is “martians”

Tintin B reentered at 08 Aug 2020
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_02207D65342C6E063455</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">M1400 Paz launch groundtrack
</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Estimated track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 22-Feb-18 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b3/4 Flight 49 - VAFB SLC-4E

First flight with fairing 2.0.
Sooty expendable legless booster 1038.2, AL type of grid fins.

Totally 2150kg payload - 1350kg Paz (ex SEOSAR) satellite with two 400kg Starlink demo satellites MicroSat-2a/2b (Tintin A/B)

Deployment into 497/517km/97.46° sun-synchronous dawn-dusk orbit

@elonmusk 22 Feb 2018:
First two Starlink demo satellites, called Tintin A &amp; B, deployed and communicating to Earth stations
Tintin A &amp; B will attempt to beam “hello world” in about 22 hours when they pass near LA
Don’t tell anyone, but the wifi password is “martians”

Tintin B reentered at 08 Aug 2020
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
