		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_1FCAC2DD6E624BE9">
			<name>M1393 Hispasat 30W-6 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1393 Hispasat 30W-6 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Estimated track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 06-Mar-18 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b4 Flight 50 - CCAFS SLC-40

Expendable booster 1044, legs and TI type of grid fins due to unfavorable weather conditions in the recovery area. Fairing 1.0
Totally 6092kg GEO satellite Hispasat 30W-6 (1F) (slot 30°W).
Secondary payload DARPA-sponsored Phoenix program experiment PODSat1 (Payload Orbital Delivery system Satellite).
Postponed from 25-Feb-18 due to additional testing on the fairing’s pressurization system.

Deployment to 184/22261km/26.97° sub-GTO orbit

@elonmusk 05 Mar 2018
Falcon 9 flight 50 launches tonight, carrying Hispasat for Spain. At 6 metric tons and almost the size of a city bus, it will be the largest geostationary satellite we’ve ever flown.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_02207D65342C6E063455</styleUrl>
