		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2132854DC662D96D">
			<name>M1418 Bangabandhu-1 launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1418 Bangabandhu-1 launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 11-May-18 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 Flight 54 - KSC LC-39A

Booster 1046

3750kg GEO satellite (slot 119.1°E).

Deployment to 308/35549km/19.31° GTO orbit

First flight of Falcon v1.2.b5 (Falcon v6) - Final reliability/reusability substantional upgrade - Retractable landin legs v2, Ti GridFins, Higher strength series 7000 aluminium bolted octaweb 3.0, Thermally shielded black design of interstage,legs,raceway, CrewConfM1D with redesigned turbopumps-higher thrust (190k lbf S1, 220k lbf S2), Base water cooled titanium heat shield, Upgraded avionics, Easy to reuse - aimed within 24 hours, qualified for 10+ flights.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0B154E8C3F2C6E06345F</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">M1418 Bangabandhu-1 launch groundtrack</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/L9HXtj

Launch - 11-May-18 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 Flight 54 - KSC LC-39A

Booster 1046

3750kg GEO satellite (slot 119.1°E).

Deployment to 308/35549km/19.31° GTO orbit

First flight of Falcon v1.2.b5 (Falcon v6) - Final reliability/reusability substantional upgrade - Retractable landin legs v2, Ti GridFins, Higher strength series 7000 aluminium bolted octaweb 3.0, Thermally shielded black design of interstage,legs,raceway, CrewConfM1D with redesigned turbopumps-higher thrust (190k lbf S1, 220k lbf S2), Base water cooled titanium heat shield, Upgraded avionics, Easy to reuse - aimed within 24 hours, qualified for 10+ flights.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
