		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2729DB1EDDF0650F">
			<name>M1384 PSN-6 real ASDS position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1384 PSN-6 real ASDS position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 22-Feb-19 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 B1048.3 Flight 68 - Marmac304 OCISLY, Signet Warhorse III tug, Go Quest support

Signet Warhorse III tug MarineTraffic recovery position.
674km downrange, from initially plannned position 19 km southeast

MECO at 2336m/s, 1-3-1 engines 19s entry burn, 1-3-1 engines ~19s successful landing burn.
3m from bullseye landing, secured by Octograbber (four arms deployed) .

@elonmusk 22 Feb 2019:
Highest reentry heating to date. Burning metal sparks from base heat shield visible in landing video. Fourth relight scheduled for April.
Crew Dragon high altitude abort test
</div>]]></description>
