			<name>M1392 Arabsat-6A (FH-02) launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1392 Arabsat-6A (FH-02) launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/HXcS8Q

Launch - 11-Apr-19 - Falcon Heavy b5 Flight 2 - KSC LC-39A

CC-B1055, NY-B1052, PY-B1053, Fairing 2.1. (with extra thermal protection on the tip), All boosters and S2 with COPV 2.0

First fligth of Block5 FH. First commercial flight of FH.

6465kg GEO satellite (slot 30.5°E).

Deployment to 321/89808km/22.96°super STO

@elonmusk 05 Apr 2019:
Static fire data looks good so far. This is first launch of Falcon Heavy Block 5, so we’re being extra cautious. Launch date might move.
Max thrust of 2550 tons will be almost 10% higher than Falcon Heavy demo mission last year
@elonmusk 10 Apr 2019:
First flight for Falcon Heavy Block 5 means there is some risk of failure between 5% to 10% imo. Many good design improvements from Falcon Heavy demo, but the changes are unproven.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_05907649AE2C6E06345D</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
