		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_285BBB199507F407">
			<name>M1405 CRS-17 ASDS position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1405 CRS-17 ASDS position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 04-May-19 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 Flight 70 B1056 - Marmac304 OCISLY, Hollywood tug, Go Quest support

20km offshore

FCC APPLICATION: http://bit.do/91679

Formerly planned landing to LZ-1 http://bit.do/89957 is cancelled due to Crew Dragon static fire failure on LZ-1 20-Apr-19.

MECO at 1581m/s. 1-3-1 engines 55s boostback burn, 1-3-1 engines 23s entry burn, single engine 33s succesful landing burn.
3m from bullseye landing, secured by all arms of Octograbber. Landing legs stowed.

@elonmusk 07 May 2019:
One of the biggest reusability improvements was fast leg stow. Version 1 sometimes took days.
</div>]]></description>
