		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_28BB76398A623FAD">
			<name>M1488 Starlink-1 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1488 Starlink-1 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/HXcS8Q

Launch - 24-May-19 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 Flight 71 - CCAFS SLC-40

Booster 1049.3, fairing 2.1-s. (tip thermal protection) without acoustic tiles

First demonstration set of 60pcs SpaceX Starlink v0.9 satellites (227 kg each) on target orbit approx. 550/550km/53°
Totally 16,783kg payload
Deployment to 433/442.5km/53.02° orbit

@elonmusk 12 May 2019
First 60 @SpaceX Starlink satellites loaded into Falcon fairing. Tight fit.
It is flat-packed. No dispenser.
@elonmusk 16 May 2019
Starlink mission will be heaviest @SpaceX payload ever at 18.5 tons. If all goes well, each launch of 60 satellites will generate more power than Space Station & deliver 1 terabit of bandwidth to Earth.
6 more launches of 60 satellites for initial activation, 12 for significant coverage
@elonmusk 24 May 2019
All 60 Starlink satellites online, solar array deployment coming up soon
Krypton ion thrusters activate in about 3 hours to raise orbit
@elonmusk 25 May 2019
Krypton thrusters operative, satellites initiating orbit raise every 90 mins
</div>]]></description>
