		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2987A73EBE904E09">
			<name>STP-2 (FH-03) launch groundtrack</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: STP-2 (FH-03) launch groundtrack</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas https://goo.gl/HXcS8Q

Launch - 25-Jun-19 - Falcon Heavy b5 Flight 3 - KSC LC-39A

CC-B1057, NY-B1052.2, PY-B1053.2, Fairing 2.1. (tip thermal protection), All boosters and S2 with COPV 2.0.

3700kg LEO/MEO 24 DoD Space Test Program 2 satellites
First time relight of M1D Vac for the fourth times.

Deployment to 306/852/28.5° - Oculus-ASR; PPOD1 - TEPCE 1&2; PPOD2 - FalconSat-7; PPOD3 - ARMADILLO; PPOD4 - PSat-2, BRICSat-2; PPOD5 - Prometheus 2.5; PPOD6 - E-TBEx A; PPOD7 - E-TBEx B; PPOD8 - CP-9 (LEO), StangSat
Deployment to 710/725km/24° - Prox-1, LightSail-B; NPSat-1; OTB-1; GPIM; COSMIC 2-5; COSMIC 2-6; COSMIC 2-2; COSMIC 2-4; COSMIC 2-1; COSMIC 2-3
Deployment to 5995/12010km/42.2° - DSX

@elonmusk 19 Jun 2019:
This will be our most difficult launch ever
@elonmusk 26 Jun 2019:
...we couldn’t take a chance on 2nd stage failing it’s 4th maneuver. This mission was more complex than anything I’m aware of in history of rockets. RIP center core, you did your duty well.
</div>]]></description>
