		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_29814BC8DE092BCD">
			<name>STP-2 (FH-03) ASDS position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: STP-2 (FH-03) ASDS position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 25-Jun-19 - FH v1.2.b5 Flight 3 CenterCore-B1057 - Marmac304 OCISLY, Hollywood tug, Go Quest support

1236 km downrange

FCC APPLICATION: http://bit.do/93066

MECO at 3052m/s, 1-3-1 engines 13s entry burn, 1-3-1 engines 12s landing burn.
Landing unsuccesful. Center core exploded out of droneship during landing burn.

@elonmusk 25 Jun 2019:
Center core RUD. It was a long shot.
High payload/delta-V missions will always be far downrange. Value of boost stage is measured (essentially) by *horizontal* velocity imparted to upper stage. Altitude is almost unimportant.
@elonmusk 26 Jun 2019:
High entry force & heat breached engine bay & center engine TVC failed
...we couldn’t take a chance on 2nd stage failing it’s 4th maneuver. This mission was more complex than anything I’m aware of in history of rockets. RIP center core, you did your duty well.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_05657893312C6E063460</styleUrl>
