		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2D26F4BAA61BBFF2">
			<name>M1429 JCSat-18 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1429 JCSat-18 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: GO Ms.Tree and GO Ms. Chief MarineTraffic recovery position.

790km downrange

New fairing 2.1. (tip thermal protection).
Ms. Tree and Ms. Chief narrowly missed catching the fairing halves.

Active fairing half recovered from the water by GO Ms.Tree. Then used only as practice fairing.
Passive fairing half recovered from the water by GO Ms.Chief.

@elonmusk 17 Dec 2019:
Sigh …
Telemetry indicates soft touchdown on the water, so fairing might still be reusable
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0A6A2036232C6E063458</styleUrl>
