		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2D18A33970BA9233">
			<name>M1357 CCP-IFAT launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1357 CCP-IFAT launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Launch hazard areas http://bit.do/LHA10

Launch - 19-Jan-20 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 Flight 79 - KSC LC-39A

Expendable legless Booster 1046.4, no grid fins. Stage2 with Mvac simulator (no engine)

Crew Dragon C205 CCP High Altitude In-Flight Abort Test

F9 simulated a loss of thrust scenario at T+85sec, 536 m/s and 19km altitude - LAS autonomously detected min-acceleration and trigered abort to command F9 to shut down, then separated himself by firing SuperDraco LAS for 7 sec to accererate from 540 m/s to 675 m/s.
Reached max.speed 2.3Mach, achieved altitude 40km.

Two Anthropomorphic Test Devices (ATD), 3 cargo rack as cargo bags ballast, no floor, mass simulator of life support components.

@elonmusk 22 Feb 2019:
High probability of this particular rocket getting destroyed by Dragon supersonic abort test.
Upper stage is flight, except mass sim in place of Merlin. It will get fragged for sure by aero loads & Dragon abort thrusters.
@elonmusk 12 Jan 2020:
We tried to design a way to save B1046, but not possible
Destroyed in Dragon fire
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0B154E8C3F2C6E06345F</styleUrl>
