		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2D233764948FD6FD">
			<name>M1357 CCP-IFAT booster debris splashdown
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1357 CCP-IFAT booster debris splashdown
</div><div><b>description</b>: Center of booster debris splashdown estimated according to Monte Carlo Model.

Splash down - 19-Jan-20 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 B1046.4 (Expendable) Flight 79

Approx. 15.3km downrange

Monte Carlo Model of Debris Relative to Dragon Landing Dispersed Ellipse

The separation of Dragon from F9 at T+85sec. Falcon broken apart due to the tumbling. Intact S2 with attached interstage impacted ocean.

SpaceX plans to recover all floating debris.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_04DA77D1A72C6E063461</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
