</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Center of booster debris splashdown estimated according to Monte Carlo Model.

Splash down - 19-Jan-20 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 B1046.4 (Expendable) Flight 79

Approx. 15.3km downrange

Monte Carlo Model of Debris Relative to Dragon Landing Dispersed Ellipse

The separation of Dragon from F9 at T+85sec. Falcon broken apart due to the tumbling. Intact S2 with attached interstage impacted ocean.

SpaceX plans to recover all floating debris.
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
