		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2AF78FEC71E42205">
			<name>M1502 Starlink_v1.0-L4 ASDS position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1502 Starlink_v1.0-L4 ASDS position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 17-Feb-20 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 - Flight 81 B1056.4 - Marmac304 OCISLY, Hawk tug, Go Quest support

629km downrange (Radius of operation within 75km)

FCC APPLICATION: http://bit.do/94661

MECO at 2184m/s, 1-3-1 engines ~23s entry burn, single engine ~27s landing burn.
Landing failure due to the unpredicted gust of wind - diverting to a water landing.
Later it was likely sunk at sea.

Hans Koenigsmann 06 Mar 2020:
Last launch had a landing failure due to the winds that the booster encountered not being as predicted. Therefore, the booster decided to divert to a water landing to protect the droneship.
</div>]]></description>
