		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_32154C59AF72F444">
			<name>M1516 Starlink_v1.0-L10 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1516 Starlink_v1.0-L10 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: GO Ms.Tree and GO Ms. Chief MarineTraffic recovery position.

707km downrange

Fairing 2.1-s (tip thermal protection) without acoustic tiles.

The fairing halves previously flew on the Starlink_v1.0-L3 mission launch in Jan 2020

Intact active fairing half captured to the net of GO Ms.Tree.
Intact passive fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Ms.Chief.

@SpaceX 18 Aug 2020:
Ms. Tree caught a Falcon 9 fairing half!
@elonmusk 18 Aug 2020:
Ms Tree catches fairing in her net
Fairing chute control & ship control are closing the loop locally. Both operating on (SpaceX) autopilot.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0A6A2036232C6E063458</styleUrl>
