			<name>M1442 SXM-7 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1442 SXM-7 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: GO Ms.Tree and GO Searcher MarineTraffic recovery position.

795km downrange

Fairing 2.2 (tip thermal protection, lowered square protrusion).

Second reflight for passive fairing half (after Anasis-II).
No fairing catch attempt by Ms.Chief, as undergoing upgrades.

@SpaceX 08 Dec 2020:
Falcon 9’s first stage previously supported six missions and one of its fairing halves previously flew on the ANASIS-II mission

Intact active fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Ms.Tree.
Intact passive fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Searcher.
</div>]]></description>
