		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_34F3EE12B949D1C4">
			<name>M1453 Turksat-5A fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1453 Turksat-5A fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: GO Ms.Tree and GO Ms. Chief MarineTraffic recovery position.

845km downrange

Fairing 2.2 (tip thermal protection, lowered square protrusion).

Second reflight for active fairing half (after Anasis-II). Second reflight for passive fairing half (after GPS III SV03).

SpaceX 07 Jan 2021:
One half previously supported the GPS III Space Vehicle 03 mission and the other flew aboard the ANASIS-II mission.

Attempt to catch one fairing half in the air with Ms. Chief, while Ms. Tree plans to retrieve the other half from the water.

Damaged active fairing half by unsuccessful catch attempt by GO Ms.Chief.
Intact passive fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Ms.Tree.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0A6A2036232C6E063458</styleUrl>
