</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Middle track inside hazard areas http://bit.do/LHA13

Launch - 24-Jan-21 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 Flight 106 - CCSFS SLC-40

Booster 1058.5, fairing 2.2-se.

~5000kg Transporter-1 SmallSat Rideshare payload with 143 commercial and government spacecraft (including CubeSats, microsats, and orbital transfer vehicles) and 10 Starlink satellites
Most spacecraft ever deployed on a single mission.
First dedicated rideshare by SpaceX. Starlink satellites aboard this mission is first in the constellation to deploy to a polar orbit.

Deployment into approx. 530/543km/97.5° SSO orbit
Stage2 debris reentry during second orbit in South Pacific.

@elonmusk 23 Jan 2021:
Launching many small satellites for a wide range of customers tomorrow. Excited about offering low-cost access to orbit for small companies!
@elonmusk 25 Jan 2021:
These also have laser links between the satellites, so no ground stations are needed over the poles
All sats launched next year will have laser links. Only our polar sats have lasers this year &amp; are v0.9.
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
