		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_3586CC9A7456CAFB">
			<name>SRFM2-1 Starlink_v1.0-L19 ASDS position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: SRFM2-1 Starlink_v1.0-L19 ASDS position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Landing - 16-Feb-21 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5- Flight 108 B1059.6 - Marmac304 OCISLY, Hawk tug, Go Quest support

634km downrange (Radius of operation within 75km)

FCC APPLICATION: http://bit.do/104483

MECO at 2203m/s, apogee 116km, 1-3-1 engines 23s entry burn at alt 54-33km, reentry at 1633m/s.
Booster landing failure.

SpaceX’s Benji Reed: An anomaly during the recent Starlink mission was due to a boot having a hole in it during ascent. An engine was shutdown safely as a result. The mission continued on successfully due to the multi-engine out capability on Falcon 9, but the landing was not possible due to the engine's issue. This particular component was a flight-leading piece of hardware. They will fix this issue moving forward with updated refurbishment processes.
</div>]]></description>
