FCC APPLICATION: http://bit.do/104483

MECO at 2203m/s, apogee 116km, 1-3-1 engines 23s entry burn at alt 54-33km, reentry at 1633m/s.
Booster landing failure.

SpaceX’s Benji Reed: An anomaly during the recent Starlink mission was due to a boot having a hole in it during ascent. An engine was shutdown safely as a result. The mission continued on successfully due to the multi-engine out capability on Falcon 9, but the landing was not possible due to the engine&apos;s issue. This particular component was a flight-leading piece of hardware. They will fix this issue moving forward with updated refurbishment processes.
