		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_36102CF85891B8A0">
			<name>M1545 Starlink_v1.0-L17 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1545 Starlink_v1.0-L17 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: GO Searcher and GO Navigator MarineTraffic recovery positions.

665km downrange

Fairing 2.1/2.2-set (lowered square protrusion of passive half) without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges, no tip thermal protection.

Spx: One half of Falcon 9’s fairing previously flew on three Starlink missions, and the other half previously supported two Starlink missions.

Fourth reflight for active fairing half (after Starlink_v0.9, Starlink_v1.0-L5 and Starlink_v1.0-L12).
Third reflight for passive fairing half (after Starlink_v1.0-L7 and Starlink_v1.0-L15).

Intact passive fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Searcher
Intact active fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Navigator
</div>]]></description>
