		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_3634E90ECDBD2503">
			<name>SRFM3-1 Starlink_v1.0-L20 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: SRFM3-1 Starlink_v1.0-L20 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: GO Searcher and GO Navigator MarineTraffic recovery positions.

667km downrange

Fairing 2.2-se (tip thermal protection, lowered square protrusion) without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges.

Second reflight for active fairing half (after Sentinel-6 MF).
Third reflight for passive fairing half (after ANASIS-II and SXM-7).

Spx: One half of Falcon 9’s fairing previously flew on the ANASIS-II and SXM-7 missions, and the other half previously supported launch of Sentinel-6A.
Planned wet recovery - retrieving each half from the water.

Intact active fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Navigator.
Intact passive fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Searcher.
Both fairing halves later transported from NC to the Cape by GO Pursuit.
</div>]]></description>
