		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_3679849C18C22D7B">
			<name>SRFM5-1 Starlink_v1.0-L22 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: SRFM5-1 Starlink_v1.0-L22 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Shelia Bordelon MarineTraffic recovery position.

692km downrange

Fairing 2.2-set (lowered square protrusion) without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges, no tip thermal protection.

Spx: One half of Falcon 9’s fairing supported the Sentinel-6A mission and the other supported a previous Starlink mission.

Second reflight for active fairing half.
Second reflight for passive fairing half (after Sentinel-6 MF).

Intact active and passive fairing halves scooped out from the water by Shelia Bordelon
</div>]]></description>
