		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_36C12E2A9386BED6">
			<name>SRFM6-1 Starlink_v1.0-L23 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: SRFM6-1 Starlink_v1.0-L23 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Shelia Bordelon MarineTraffic recovery position.

670km downrange

Fairing 2.1/2.2-set (lowered square protrusion of passive half) without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges, no tip thermal protection.

Spx: One half of Falcon 9’s fairing previously supported launch of AMOS-17 and two Starlink missions, and the other previously supported a Starlink mission.

Fourth reflight for active fairing half (after Amos-17,Starl1-L6 and Starl1-L15).
Second reflight for passive fairing half (after Starl1-L12?).

Intact active fairing half scooped out from the water by Shelia Bordelon
</div>]]></description>
