		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_3789ED7367BF15B6">
			<name>Starlink_v1.0-L26 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Starlink_v1.0-L26 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Fairing 2.2-se (tip thermal protection, lowered square protrusion) without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges.

Shelia Bordelon MarineTraffic recovery position 681km downrange

Spx: One half of Falcon 9’s fairing previously supported the SXM-7 mission, and the other previously supported the NROL-108 mission.

Second flight for active fairing half (after SXM-7).
Second flight for passive fairing half (after NROL-108).

Intact active fairing half scooped out from the water by Shelia Bordelon
</div>]]></description>
