</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">GO Searcher and GO Navigator water recovery.

MarineTraffic recovery position 667km downrange

Fairing 2.1/2.2-set (lowered square protrusion of passive half) without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges, no tip thermal protection.

Spx: One half of Falcon 9’s fairing previously supported four Starlink missions, and the other previously supported a Starlink mission and the Transporter-1 mission.

Fifth flight for active fairing half (after Starlink-1 v0.9, Star1-L5, Star1-L12, Star1-L17).
Third flight for passive fairing half (after Transporter-1 and Star1-L21).

Intact active fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Navigator
Intact passive fairing half scooped out from the water by GO Searcher

@SpaceX 26 May 2021
Today&apos;s flight will mark the 40th time SpaceX has reflown Falcon fairing halves since November 2019
This will also be the first time we fly a fairing half on its fifth mission
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
