		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_3A0050A8C3351825">
			<name>SRFM1-5 Starlink_G2-1 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: SRFM1-5 Starlink_G2-1 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Middle track inside hazard areas http://bit.do/LHA15

Launch - 14-Sep -21 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 - Flight 125 - VSFB SLC-4E

Booster 1049.10, Fairing 2.2-se.

Totally 15637kg payload. 51pcs SpaceX Starlink v1.5 satellites with laser intersatellite links (306.6 kg each) on target orbit approx. 570/570km/70°

Planned nominal deployment to 219.8/350.1km/70° orbit.
Stage2 debris reentry reentry on the first orbit in northwestern Indian Ocean.

@elonmusk 11 Sep 2021:
These are V1.5 Starlinks with laser inter-satellite links, which are needed for high latitudes & mid ocean coverage
</div>]]></description>
