		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_3EBC9F2073AF6F94">
			<name>M1779 Starlink_G4-17 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1779 Starlink_G4-17 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Roughly estimated Doug recovery position 643km downrange
Fairing Fairing 2.1-2.2-se. (without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges).

Sixth flight for active fairing half (after Amos-17,Starl1-L6, Starl1-L15, Starl1-L23 and Starlink_G4-5).
Third flight for passive fairing half (after Starlink_v1-L25 and Starlink_G4-1).

SpX webcast: "one of the fairing halves today protecting our Starlink satellites today will be flying for its third time while the other fairing half is flying for the sixth time"

Intact active and passive fairing halves scooped out from the water by Doug.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0A6A2036232C6E063458</styleUrl>
