		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_411F763F5281CAAD">
			<name>M1785 Starlink_G4-23 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1785 Starlink_G4-23 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Ground track based on hazard areas http://bit.do/LHA19

Launch - 28-Aug-22 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 - Flight 172 - CCSFS SLC-40

Booster B1069.2, Fairing 2.3-s.

Totally 16700kg payload. 54pcs SpaceX Starlink v1.5 satellites with laser intersatellite links (309 kg each), on target orbit approx. 540/540km/53.2°
Highest ever payload mass to orbit on recoverable F9.

Planned nominal deployment to 239/343.6km/53.22° orbit.
Stage2 debris reentry in eastern Pacific on the first orbit..

@elonmusk 28 Aug 2022:
Squeezing extra performance out of Falcon 9 – almost at 17 metric tons to an actual useful orbit with booster & fairing reusable!
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0B154E8C3F2C6E06345F</styleUrl>
