		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_41494F7F7977A2C0">
			<name>M1714 Starlink_G4-2 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1714 Starlink_G4-2 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Ground track based on hazard areas http://bit.do/LHA20

Launch - 10-Sep-22 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 - Flight 175 - KSC LC-39A

Booster B1058.14 - first 14th reflight of booster, Fairing 2.3-s/2.2.-se

Totally ~12006kg payload. 34pcs SpaceX Starlink v1.5 satellites with laser intersatellite links (309 kg each) on target orbit approx. 540/540km/53.2° and BlueWalker 3 (1500 kg), on target orbit approx. 513/513km/53°

Planned nominal deployment to 331.6/340.9km/53.21° orbit.
Stage2 debris reentry in southern Pacific on the second orbit.

@elonmusk 09 Sep 2022:
One of our most complex missions (5 burns on the second stage)
No obvious limit to rocket reflight so far
</div>]]></description>
