		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_42A02227E100EDC9">
			<name>M1802 Intelsat G31/32 fairing recovery position
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1802 Intelsat G31/32 fairing recovery position
</div><div><b>description</b>: Bob MarineTraffic recovery position 959km downrange

Fairing 2.2-se (without acoustic tiles, vent holes at halves edges).

Fifth flight for active fairing half (after GPS III SV04, Starlink_v1-L27, Starlink_G4-1 and Starlink_G4-12).
Fifth flight for passive fairing half (after Starlink_v1-L7, Starlink_v1-L15, Starlink_v1-L17 and Starlink_G4-5).

SpX webcast: "both of those fairing halves are flight proven, both of them flying for the fifth times"

Both intact fairing halves scooped out from the water by Bob
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0A6A2036232C6E063458</styleUrl>
