		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_44AAAF2299BA8FF0">
			<name>M1887 Starlink_G6-1 launch groundtrack
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: M1887 Starlink_G6-1 launch groundtrack
</div><div><b>description</b>: Ground track based on hazard areas and SpX webcast http://bit.ly/LHA-23

Launch - 27-Feb-23 - Falcon 9 v1.2.b5 - Flight 206 - CCSFS SLC-40

Booster B1076.3, Fairing 2.3-s.

21pcs SpaceX Starlink v2 Mini satellites.
 First flight of Starlink v2 Mini satellites with more powerful phased array antennas, use of E-band for backhaul, new argon Hall thrusters for on orbit maneuvering with 2.4x the thrust and 1.5x the specific impulse.
Planned nominal deployment to 372.5/380km/43° orbit.
Stage2 debris reentry during second orbit south of Cape Town.
</div>]]></description>
