		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_20661615B8D70715">
			<name>LC-39A Horizontal Integration Facility</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: LC-39A Horizontal Integration Facility</div><div><b>description</b>: F9-FH hangar at LC-39A
Size - 92x35m.

The Integration Hanger is used for final assembly of the rocket. The pieces of the rocket enter through the south end of the building and are placed on cradles located on rails for easy movement. Upon completion of the assembly, the rocket is transferred out the north door to the launch pad. In addition to rocket assembly, the Integration Hangar is also used to conduct electrical and leak testing.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_49D06F53982C6E0634BF</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">LC-39A Horizontal Integration Facility</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">F9-FH hangar at LC-39A
Size - 92x35m.

The Integration Hanger is used for final assembly of the rocket. The pieces of the rocket enter through the south end of the building and are placed on cradles located on rails for easy movement. Upon completion of the assembly, the rocket is transferred out the north door to the launch pad. In addition to rocket assembly, the Integration Hangar is also used to conduct electrical and leak testing.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
