		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_2072227ACAF363BD">
			<name>Hangar X - booster storage</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Hangar X - booster storage</div><div><b>description</b>: Hangar AO (Hangar X, Facility #60530), former Delta II hangar
Building 60530 Hangar Road, CAPE CANAVERAL, FL32920

Hangar AO is used to refurbish rockets after launch and landing in order to fly again.

Rockets are cleaned, repaired, and tested in this hangar. Cleaning involves using isopropyl alcohol (IPA) on a rag or wipe. Repair involves touch up painting using a variety of 2-part epoxies. Testing involves checking electronic and mechanical systems for proper operation.

Size - 61x16m.
Space for two F9 v1.2. S1 included interstage.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_300BB4EA472C6E0634C6</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Hangar X - booster storage</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Hangar AO (Hangar X, Facility #60530), former Delta II hangar
Building 60530 Hangar Road, CAPE CANAVERAL, FL32920

Hangar AO is used to refurbish rockets after launch and landing in order to fly again.

Rockets are cleaned, repaired, and tested in this hangar. Cleaning involves using isopropyl alcohol (IPA) on a rag or wipe. Repair involves touch up painting using a variety of 2-part epoxies. Testing involves checking electronic and mechanical systems for proper operation.

Size - 61x16m.
Space for two F9 v1.2. S1 included interstage.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
