		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_277287CD3FFF8C2A">
			<name>Starship Suborbital Pad A</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Starship Suborbital Pad A</div><div><b>description</b>: 04 Jun 2022 - S24 installed onto pad A
13 May 2022 - S24 removed from pad A
08 Jan 2022 - BN3 LOX section disassembled in-situ at the Pad A.
14 Aug 2021 - BN3 CH4 section disassembled in-situ at the Pad A.
20 Jul 2021 - 3 Raptors Static Fire of Super Heavy Booster 3
@elonmusk 20 Jul 2021:
Full test duration firing of 3 Raptors on Super Heavy Booster!

01 Jul 2021 - Super Heavy Booster 3 installed

05 May 2021 - Starship SN15 10km successful Flight Test.
@elonmusk 05 May 2021:
Starship landing nominal!

27 Apr 2021 - Starship SN15 header tank Static Fire test.
@elonmusk 28 Apr 2021:
Testing header tanks. All good so far.
26 Apr 2021 - Starship SN15 tripple Raptor Static Fire test.
@elonmusk 27 Apr 2021:
Starhip SN15 static fire completed, preparing for flight later this week.
13 Apr 2021 - Cryogenic Proof Testing
09 Apr 2021 - Starship SN15 installed

03 Mar 2021 - Starship SN10 10km successful Flight Test. RUD shortly after landing.
@elonmusk 04 Mar 2021:
Starship SN10 landed in one piece!
SpaceX team is doing great work! One day, the true measure of success will be that Starship flights are commonplace.
RIP SN10, honorable discharge
@elonmusk 06 Mar 2021:
Thrust was low despite being commanded high for reasons unknown at present, hence hard touchdown. We’ve never seen this before.
Next time, min two engines all the way to the ground & restart engine 3 if engine 1 or 2 have issues.
This was way past leg loads. They got squashed hard.

25 Feb 2021 - SN10 Static Fire test after Raptor engine swap.
23 Feb 2021 - Starship SN10 tripple Raptor Static Fire test.
@elonmusk 24 Feb 2021:
One of the engines is suspect, so we’re swapping it out

29 Jan 2021 - fully stacked Starship SN10 installed
@elonmusk 29 Jan 2021:
Cryoproof, then install engines

09 Dec 2020 - Starship SN8 12,5 kmHigh-Altitude Flight Test - 12.5km
@elonmusk 09 Dec 2020:
Successful ascent, switchover to header tanks & precise flap control to landing point!
Fuel header tank pressure was low during landing burn, causing touchdown velocity to be high & RUD, but we got all the data we needed! Congrats SpaceX team hell yeah!!
Thank you, South Texas for your support! This is the gateway to Mars.
Mars, here we come!!
SN8 did great! Even reaching apogee would’ve been great, so controlling all way to putting the crater in the right spot was epic!!

24 Nov 2020 - Starship SN8 triple Raptor static fire.
@elonmusk 25 Nov 2020:
Good Starship SN8 static fire! Aiming for first 15km / ~50k ft altitude flight next week. Goals are to test 3 engine ascent, body flaps, transition from main to header tanks & landing flip.
Lot of things need to go right, so maybe 1/3 chance
But that’s why we have SN 9 & SN10

13 Nov 2020 - Starship SN8 double Raptor static fire from the header tanks. 
@elonmusk 13 Nov 2020:
We lost vehicle pneumatics. Reason unknown at present. Liquid oxygen header tank pressure is rising. Hopefully triggers burst disk to relieve pressure, otherwise it’s going to pop the cork.
Maybe melted an engine preburner or fuel hot gas manifold. Whatever it is caused pneumatics loss. We need to design out this problem.
Burst disk worked, so vehicle appears to be ok. We’ll have to swap out at least one of the engines.
@elonmusk 14 Nov 2020:
Just a scratch. We can buff it out.
@elonmusk 17 Nov 2020:
About 2 secs after starting engines, martyte covering concrete below shattered, sending blades of hardened rock into engine bay. One rock blade severed avionics cable, causing bad shutdown of Raptor.
Avionics cables moving to steel pipe shields & adding water-cooled steel pipes to test pad

11 Nov 2020 - Starship SN8 single Raptor successful static fire using the Nosecone LOX Header Tank. 
04 Nov 2020 - Starship SN8 LOX Header Proof Test 
23 Oct 2020 - fully stacked Starship SN8 with nosecone installed

20 Oct 2020 - SN8 multi-raptor pre-burner & successful static fire test
@elonmusk 21 Oct 2020:
Data from 3 engine Starship static fire this morning looks good. Proceeding with nosecone mate.

19 Oct 2020 - SN8 multi-raptor pre-burner test

09 Oct 2020 - SN8 successful cryo pressure test
@elonmusk 09 Oct 2020:
Passed cryo proof

07 Oct 2020 - SN8 cryo pressure test
@elonmusk 07 Oct 2020:
Cryo pressure test succeeded, but a small leak opened up near the engine mounts, possibly due to differential shrinking

26 Sep 2020 - Starship SN8 on test stand
@elonmusk 26 Sep 2020:
Starship SN8 with rear body flaps
Nosecone & front flaps next week. SN9 next month.
First flight is to 15km or ~50,000 ft

07 Sep 2020 - Starship SN6 removed from stand
03 Sep 2020 - Starship SN6 150m flight test
@elonmusk 04 Sep 2020:
Starship SN6 flew asimilar hop to SN5, but it was a much smoother & faster operation

24 Aug 2020 - SN6 successful static fire with SN29 Raptor
11 Aug 2020 - Starship SN6 on test stand
11 Aug 2020 - Starship SN5 removed from stand
05 Aug 2020 - SN5 150 meter test hop
@elonmusk 05 Aug 2020: Mars is looking real

30 Jul 2020 - SN5 successful static fire
@elonmusk 30 Jul 2020:
Starship SN5 just completed full duration static fire. 150m hop soon.

22 Jul 2020 - SN5 successful tanking test
04 Jul 2020 - SN27 Raptor Installed
01 Jul 2020 - SN5 successful cryo proof test
24 Jun 2020 - Starship SN5 tank on test stand

Elon Musk 31 May 2020: "Unfortunately what we thought was going to be a minor test of a quick disconnect ended up being a big problem"

29 May 2020 - SN4 exploded after static fire
28 May 2020 - SN4 static fire
19 May 2020 - SN4 static fire
17 May 2020 - SN4 preburner ignition

@elonmusk 10 May 2020:
SN4 passed high pressure (7.5 bar) & engine thrust load at cryo

07 May 2020 - 2nd SN4 static fire
@elonmusk 07 May 2020:
Yes. Static fire feeding from fuel header vs main tank.

06 May 2020 - SN4 static fire
@elonmusk 06 May 2020:
Starship SN4 passed static fire

05 May 2020 - SN4 preburner test.

@elonmusk 27 Apr 2020:
Cryo test underway
Snowing in Texas
SN4 passed cryo proof!
4.9 bar. Kind of a softball tbh, but that’s enough to fly!
Static fire with Raptor hopefully later this week
Just one. SN5 will get three.

@elonmusk 26 Apr 2020:
SN4 passed ambient pressure test
Aiming for cryo pressure test tonight

23 Apr 2020 - SN4 tank lifted onto test stand

@elonmusk 23 Apr 2020:
Starship SN4 tank on test stand

03 Apr 2020 - SN3 collapsed at cryo pressurization testing

@elonmusk 03 Apr 2020:
We will see what data review says in the morning, but this may have been a test configuration mistake

29 Mar 2020 - SN3 lifted onto the launch mount

08 Mar 2020 - successfull nondestructive tank cryo test by flight pressures, including simulated engine thrust loads

28 Feb 2020 - SN1 tank cryo proof test failure

25 Feb 2020 - SN1 (Mk3) Tank Section on place

29 Jan 2020 - tank destructive test by 8.5 bar (1.4x safety factor over the 6 bar requirement)

10 Jan 2020 - tank destructive test by 7.1 bar (above 6 bar required for orbital flight)

21 Nov 2019 - Top bulkhead of Mk1 blew off during a pressure test to the max.

@elonmusk 21 Nov 2019:
Absolutely, but to move to Mk3 design. This had some value as a manufacturing pathfinder, but flight design is quite differen

Since 30 Oct 2019 - Bottom section of StarShip Mk1 Orbital Prototype

Formerly Starship Hopper in development:

Until 27 Aug 2019
Removed to Landing Pad by 150 Meter Starhopper Test

@elonmusk 26 Jul 2019:
Starhopper flight successful. Water towers *can* fly haha!!

@elonmusk 07 Jul 2019:
Exciting progress in Boca! Hopper almost ready to hover. Based on tonight’s test, looks like 600 Hz Raptor vibration problem is fixed.

@elonmusk 06 Apr 2019:
Starhopper just lifted off & hit tether limits!

@elonmusk 04 Apr 2019
Starhopper completed tethered hop. All systems green.

@elonmusk 17 Mar 2019
First (really short) hops with one engine. Suborbital flights with three.
Hopefully. Always many issues integrating engine & stage. First hops will lift off, but only barely.

16 Mar 2019 - Raptor SN02 installed

Since 08 Mar 2019
Bottom section of stainless steel Starship suborbital VTOL test hopper

@elonmusk 08 Mar 2019:
Raptor on way to Hopper. Will be mounted to vehicle next week.
04 Jun 2022 - S24 installed onto pad A
13 May 2022 - S24 removed from pad A</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_03AFFDBFE22C6E0634D8</styleUrl>
