		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_324E64ABA0E5BD7E">
			<name>Starship Suborbital Pad B</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Starship Suborbital Pad B</div><div><b>description</b>: 27 Jun 2023 - S25 six engine static fire test
15 Dec 2022 - S24 single-engine static fire test
30 Sep 2022 - Starship SN24 removed from pad B
08 Sep 2022 - Starship SN24 6-engine Static Fire test.
06 Jul 2022 - S24 installed onto pad B
29 Dec 2021 - Starship SN20 Static Fire test.
12 Nov 2021 - Starship SN20 six Raptor Static Fire test.
@elonmusk 12 Nov 2021:
Good static fire with all six engines!
22 Oct 2021 - Ship SN20 Raptor vacuum engine double static firing
@elonmusk 22 Oct 2021:
First firing of a Raptor vacuum engine integrated onto a Starship
Raptor has a very high chamber pressure, which in turn allows for a large expansion ratio nozzle without flow separation at sea level
Currently at ~270 bar, but working on upgrades to get it over 300 bar
30 Sep 2021 - Cryogenic Proof Testing
18 Aug 2021 - Ship SN20 installed on Pad B
26 May 2021 - Starship SN15 uninstalled
15 May 2021 - Starship SN15 installed
30 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 10km Flight Test. RUD in landing burn.
@elonmusk 05 Apr 2021:
Ascent phase, transition to horizontal & control during free fall were good. 
A (relatively) small CH4 leak led to fire on engine 2 & fried part of avionics, causing hard start attempting landing burn in CH4 turbopump.
 
26 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 single Raptor Static Fire test.
22 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 tripple Raptor Static Fire test.
15 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 aborted Static Fire
08 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 installed

02 Feb 2021 - Starship SN9 10 km Flight Test
22 Jan 2021 - SN9 short static fire + full duration static fire test after an engine swap
13 Jan 2021 - SN9 Three Times Raptor Engine Static Fires Tests in One Day
@elonmusk 13 Jan 2021:
Today at SpaceX is about practicing Starship engine starts. Ship is held down by massive pins while engines are fired. Two starts completed, about to try a third.
All three static fires completed & no RUDs!
Detanking & inspections now. Good progress towards our “Hop in & go to Mars!” goal

06 Jan 2021 - SN9 conducted a triple Raptor Static Fire test. 
29 Dec 2020 - SN9 passed cryogenic tank test and RCS thrusters test
22 Dec 2020 - fully stacked Starship SN9 installed
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_03AFFDBFE22C6E0634D8</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Starship Suborbital Pad B</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">27 Jun 2023 - S25 six engine static fire test
15 Dec 2022 - S24 single-engine static fire test
30 Sep 2022 - Starship SN24 removed from pad B
08 Sep 2022 - Starship SN24 6-engine Static Fire test.
06 Jul 2022 - S24 installed onto pad B
29 Dec 2021 - Starship SN20 Static Fire test.
12 Nov 2021 - Starship SN20 six Raptor Static Fire test.
@elonmusk 12 Nov 2021:
Good static fire with all six engines!
22 Oct 2021 - Ship SN20 Raptor vacuum engine double static firing
@elonmusk 22 Oct 2021:
First firing of a Raptor vacuum engine integrated onto a Starship
Raptor has a very high chamber pressure, which in turn allows for a large expansion ratio nozzle without flow separation at sea level
Currently at ~270 bar, but working on upgrades to get it over 300 bar
30 Sep 2021 - Cryogenic Proof Testing
18 Aug 2021 - Ship SN20 installed on Pad B
26 May 2021 - Starship SN15 uninstalled
15 May 2021 - Starship SN15 installed
30 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 10km Flight Test. RUD in landing burn.
@elonmusk 05 Apr 2021:
Ascent phase, transition to horizontal &amp; control during free fall were good. 
A (relatively) small CH4 leak led to fire on engine 2 &amp; fried part of avionics, causing hard start attempting landing burn in CH4 turbopump.
 
26 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 single Raptor Static Fire test.
22 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 tripple Raptor Static Fire test.
15 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 aborted Static Fire
08 Mar 2021 - Starship SN11 installed

02 Feb 2021 - Starship SN9 10 km Flight Test
22 Jan 2021 - SN9 short static fire + full duration static fire test after an engine swap
13 Jan 2021 - SN9 Three Times Raptor Engine Static Fires Tests in One Day
@elonmusk 13 Jan 2021:
Today at SpaceX is about practicing Starship engine starts. Ship is held down by massive pins while engines are fired. Two starts completed, about to try a third.
All three static fires completed &amp; no RUDs!
Detanking &amp; inspections now. Good progress towards our “Hop in &amp; go to Mars!” goal

06 Jan 2021 - SN9 conducted a triple Raptor Static Fire test. 
29 Dec 2020 - SN9 passed cryogenic tank test and RCS thrusters test
22 Dec 2020 - fully stacked Starship SN9 installed
</SimpleData>
