		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_17DD85730F6ADBEC">
			<name>Control Center Area - Parcel 2
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Control Center Area - Parcel 2
</div><div><b>description</b>: SpaceX Lot 410734

Proposed Launch Control Center:
The one-story control center buildings would be approximately 14,186 ft2 and 30-45 ft in height, and would be used for command and control of the launch vehicle, payload, and ground systems during launch and test operations. Each control center building would consist primarily of several large rooms for control consoles, conference rooms, and support rooms. In addition, each facility would house office areas for site personnel.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_3E21072B902C6E0634E4</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Control Center Area - Parcel 2
</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">SpaceX Lot 410734

Proposed Launch Control Center:
The one-story control center buildings would be approximately 14,186 ft2 and 30-45 ft in height, and would be used for command and control of the launch vehicle, payload, and ground systems during launch and test operations. Each control center building would consist primarily of several large rooms for control consoles, conference rooms, and support rooms. In addition, each facility would house office areas for site personnel.
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
