		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_25EB7A3EF4513663">
			<name>Concrete jig of Starship construction</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Concrete jig of Starship construction</div><div><b>description</b>: Diameter 9m; Height 3m
Construction jig for Starship Hopper (aka BFH) & orbital Starship vehicle.
Since 11/2018

Presently on the jig:
- Starship vehicle upper section construction

Formerly on the jig:
- Hopper upper section (top section stacked with middle section) - blown over in storm
- Hopper bottom section - moved out to own legs

@elonmusk 23 Jan 2019:
I just heard. 50 mph winds broke the mooring blocks late last night & fairing was blown over. Will take a few weeks to repair.

@elonmusk Mar 17, 2019
We decided to skip building a new nosecone for Hopper. Don’t need it. What you see being built is the orbital Starship vehicle.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_68907E8E662C6E0634C2</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Concrete jig of Starship construction</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Diameter 9m; Height 3m
Construction jig for Starship Hopper (aka BFH) &amp; orbital Starship vehicle.
Since 11/2018

Presently on the jig:
- Starship vehicle upper section construction

Formerly on the jig:
- Hopper upper section (top section stacked with middle section) - blown over in storm
- Hopper bottom section - moved out to own legs

@elonmusk 23 Jan 2019:
I just heard. 50 mph winds broke the mooring blocks late last night &amp; fairing was blown over. Will take a few weeks to repair.

@elonmusk Mar 17, 2019
We decided to skip building a new nosecone for Hopper. Don’t need it. What you see being built is the orbital Starship vehicle.
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
