		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_205FE3F92420049A">
			<name>Middle Bay of Raptor Engine Test Stand</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Middle Bay of Raptor Engine Test Stand</div><div><b>description</b>: 04 Feb 2019 - first 2 second test firing of Raptor flight engine. (170 bar, 116 metric tons force - 1.14MN, ~60% power)

@elonmusk 04 Feb 2019:
First firing of Starship Raptor flight engine! So proud of great work by @SpaceX team!!
@elonmusk 07 Feb 2019:
Raptor just achieved power level needed for Starship & Super Heavy
Design requires at least 170 metric tons of force. Engine reached 172 mT & 257 bar chamber pressure with warm propellant, which means 10% to 20% more with deep cryo

IAC 2017 - 29 Sep 2017
Over 1200s of firing across 42 main engine tests.
Longest test 100s; 40s typical fot Mars landing.
Test engine operates at up to 200atm.

26 Sep 2016 - first 9 second test firing of Raptor demonstrator engine.

@elonmusk 26 Sep 2016:
SpaceX propulsion just achieved first firing of the Raptor interplanetary transport engine
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_1C112764992C6E0634F0</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Middle Bay of Raptor Engine Test Stand</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">04 Feb 2019 - first 2 second test firing of Raptor flight engine. (170 bar, 116 metric tons force - 1.14MN, ~60% power)

@elonmusk 04 Feb 2019:
First firing of Starship Raptor flight engine! So proud of great work by @SpaceX team!!
@elonmusk 07 Feb 2019:
Raptor just achieved power level needed for Starship &amp; Super Heavy
Design requires at least 170 metric tons of force. Engine reached 172 mT &amp; 257 bar chamber pressure with warm propellant, which means 10% to 20% more with deep cryo

IAC 2017 - 29 Sep 2017
Over 1200s of firing across 42 main engine tests.
Longest test 100s; 40s typical fot Mars landing.
Test engine operates at up to 200atm.

26 Sep 2016 - first 9 second test firing of Raptor demonstrator engine.

@elonmusk 26 Sep 2016:
SpaceX propulsion just achieved first firing of the Raptor interplanetary transport engine
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
