		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_28D333EF5683DFA4">
			<name>Cooling Towers</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Cooling Towers</div><div><b>description</b>: The cooling towers are located outside in the southwest portion of the facility adjacent to HT-11 Building 3117. The cooling tower is periodically inspected for leaks. If a leak is detected, the cooling tower is shut down until repaired and the water is prevented from entering the downstream storm drain. The cooling tower is maintained regularly to prevent breakdowns.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0096B16A5F2C6E0634D5</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Cooling Towers</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">The cooling towers are located outside in the southwest portion of the facility adjacent to HT-11 Building 3117. The cooling tower is periodically inspected for leaks. If a leak is detected, the cooling tower is shut down until repaired and the water is prevented from entering the downstream storm drain. The cooling tower is maintained regularly to prevent breakdowns.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
			<Polygon>
				<outerBoundaryIs>
					<LinearRing>
						<coordinates>
							-118.3290007,33.919814,0 -118.3288691,33.9198145,0 -118.3288706,33.9199169,0 -118.3289993,33.9199186,0 -118.3290007,33.919814,0 
						</coordinates>
					</LinearRing>
				</outerBoundaryIs>
			</Polygon>
		</Placemark>
		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_28D2DD4159FB8B51">
			<name>HT11 - Furnace (Oven) Building - High Temp.</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: HT11 - Furnace (Oven) Building - High Temp.</div><div><b>description</b>: 1 Rocket Rd, Hawthorne, CA 90250

HT-11 contains the Oven Building, the electrical substation, guard booth, and an adjacent tank farm. The tank farm consists of water treatment chemicals, compressed liquid argon, compressed liquid nitrogen, and a condensate recovery tank. In the Oven Building, SpaceX cures high temperature composites (nozzle layup and cure). Parts and equipment for manufacturing and metal turnings are also stored in this area.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_300BB4EA472C6E0634C6</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">HT11 - Furnace (Oven) Building - High Temp.</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">1 Rocket Rd, Hawthorne, CA 90250

HT-11 contains the Oven Building, the electrical substation, guard booth, and an adjacent tank farm. The tank farm consists of water treatment chemicals, compressed liquid argon, compressed liquid nitrogen, and a condensate recovery tank. In the Oven Building, SpaceX cures high temperature composites (nozzle layup and cure). Parts and equipment for manufacturing and metal turnings are also stored in this area.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
