		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_18073EEF100361FE">
			<name>Boring Co- Completed Hawthorne Test Tunnel</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Boring Co- Completed Hawthorne Test Tunnel</div><div><b>description</b>: Boring Co Hawthorne tunnel - from dug trench to 105 Freeway
3.66 m (12ft) diameter.
TBM is 4.25m in diameter, which gives a finished inner diameter of around 3.8m.

@elonmusk 17 Dec 2016:
Traffic is driving me nuts. Am going to build a tunnel boring machine and just start digging...
It shall be called "The Boring Company"
Boring, it's what we do
I am actually going to do this
@elonmusk 25 Jan 2017:
Exciting progress on the tunnel front. Plan to start digging in a month or so.
Starting across from my desk at SpaceX. Crenshaw and the 105 Freeway, which is 5 mins from LAX
elonmusk 29 Jan 2017:
We’re just going to figure out what it takes to improve tunneling speed by, I think, somewhere between 500 and 1,000 percent.
elonmusk 03 Feb 2017:
We want to know what it would take to get to a mile a week? Could it be possible?
@elonmusk 12 May 2017:
First tunnel for The Boring Company begins ... Full length of first tunnel will run from LAX to Culver City, Santa Monica, Westwood and Sherman Oaks. Future tunnels will cover all of greater LA.
@elonmusk 28 Oct 2017:
500 ft so far. Should be 2 miles long in three or four months and hopefully stretch the whole 405 N-S corridor from LAX to the 101 in a year or so.</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0CD508C9AA2C6E063504</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Boring Co- Completed Hawthorne Test Tunnel</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Boring Co Hawthorne tunnel - from dug trench to 105 Freeway
3.66 m (12ft) diameter.
TBM is 4.25m in diameter, which gives a finished inner diameter of around 3.8m.

@elonmusk 17 Dec 2016:
Traffic is driving me nuts. Am going to build a tunnel boring machine and just start digging...
It shall be called &quot;The Boring Company&quot;
Boring, it&apos;s what we do
I am actually going to do this
@elonmusk 25 Jan 2017:
Exciting progress on the tunnel front. Plan to start digging in a month or so.
Starting across from my desk at SpaceX. Crenshaw and the 105 Freeway, which is 5 mins from LAX
elonmusk 29 Jan 2017:
We’re just going to figure out what it takes to improve tunneling speed by, I think, somewhere between 500 and 1,000 percent.
elonmusk 03 Feb 2017:
We want to know what it would take to get to a mile a week? Could it be possible?
@elonmusk 12 May 2017:
First tunnel for The Boring Company begins ... Full length of first tunnel will run from LAX to Culver City, Santa Monica, Westwood and Sherman Oaks. Future tunnels will cover all of greater LA.
@elonmusk 28 Oct 2017:
500 ft so far. Should be 2 miles long in three or four months and hopefully stretch the whole 405 N-S corridor from LAX to the 101 in a year or so.</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
