		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_15A6A6CFE380415D">
			<name>Construction of LOX Development Tank
</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Construction of LOX Development Tank
</div><div><b>description</b>: Construction of Interplanetary Transport System Liquid Oxygen Carbon Fiber Development Prototype Tank.

12m diameter, pressure tested to 2.3atm, volume 1000m3, holds 1200 tons of LOX

10 Nov 2016 - Successful test up to 2/3 of burst pressure of the tank on an ocean barge
09 Feb 2017 - Destructive test by burst pressure - above the design pressure

2302 T Ave, Anacortes, WA 98221
Former Pacific Marine Center.
</div>]]></description>
