		<Placemark id="4c5ae659_K9SM3GZLUCKQ1077476B10FB6B07">
			<name>Space Power Facility (SPF) testing</name>
			<description><![CDATA[<div><b>name</b>: Space Power Facility (SPF) testing</div><div><b>description</b>: Thermal-Vacuum Chamber and Reverberant Acoustic Tests of Falcon fairing.
NASA Glenn Research Center -- Plum Brook Station.

@elonmusk 20 Mar 2013:
Testing separation of F9 rocket fairing (can hold a city bus) in world's largest vacuum chamber

@SpaceX 21 Jun 2018:
Crew Dragon is at @NASA’s Plum Brook Station testing facility in Ohio, home to the largest thermal vacuum chamber in the world, to demonstrate its capability to withstand the extreme temperatures and vacuum of space.
</div>]]></description>
			<styleUrl>#__managed_style_692F3EF4D42C6E0634FD</styleUrl>
			<ExtendedData>
				<SchemaData schemaUrl="#__managed_schema">
					<SimpleData name="str:bmFtZQ==">Space Power Facility (SPF) testing</SimpleData>
					<SimpleData name="str:ZGVzY3JpcHRpb24=">Thermal-Vacuum Chamber and Reverberant Acoustic Tests of Falcon fairing.
NASA Glenn Research Center -- Plum Brook Station.

@elonmusk 20 Mar 2013:
Testing separation of F9 rocket fairing (can hold a city bus) in world&apos;s largest vacuum chamber

@SpaceX 21 Jun 2018:
Crew Dragon is at @NASA’s Plum Brook Station testing facility in Ohio, home to the largest thermal vacuum chamber in the world, to demonstrate its capability to withstand the extreme temperatures and vacuum of space.
</SimpleData>
				</SchemaData>
			</ExtendedData>
			<gx:Carousel>
				<gx:Image kml:id="hosted_image_">
